    "traits": {
      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Deluge"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "A creature can provoke a waterlogged tiddalik (see Drink Abundance below) into laughing and releasing its stored water with a successful DC 25 check to Perform a joke or funny story. The tiddalik also disgorges its water automatically if it dies while waterlogged, or can voluntarily Deluge as a three-action activity that has the concentrate trait.\n\nThe mass of stored water swamps a 10-foot emanation, dealing 8d6 bludgeoning damage to creatures in the area (DC 25 basic Reflex save) and making the area 3 for 1 day. The tiddalik can't use its spit Strike or Expel Wave until it next Drinks in Abundance."
            },
            "id": "4d0d7b11-bc43-4b67-b3bb-1de528a177be",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:27.494111"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Drink Abundance"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(downtime)\n\nThe tiddalik spends a day or more drinking from a water source. If the water source is equal to or greater in volume than itself, the tiddalik consumes 5,000 gallons of water per day and becomes waterlogged. While waterlogged, it can use its spit Strike, Expel Wave, and its deluge ability, but its."
            },
